    "before": "Half-square objective is `0.5*sum((X-WH)**2)`; MSE divides twice this by observed cell count, while a norm is its square root.",
    "after": "For unweighted observed residuals R=X\u2212WH, the half-square objective is L=`0.5*sum(R**2)`. With N the number of observed cells, squared Frobenius norm is 2L, Frobenius norm is \u221a(2L), MSE is 2L/N, and RMSE is \u221a(2L/N). The public Frobenius reconstruction diagnostic maps to \u221a(2L), never L or \u221aL. Refuse an all-missing quality reduction (N=0); fractional masks require a separately stated weight/denominator convention, and non-Frobenius divergence diagnostics retain their independently checked mapping rather than inheriting these conversions.",
